# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/runtime node903
node903 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>runtime</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/runtime' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/runtime</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;SBOM generated through instrumenting the system running the software, to capture only components present in the system, as well as external call-outs or dynamically loaded components. In some contexts, this may also be referred to as an &quot;Instrumented&quot; or &quot;Dynamic&quot; SBOM.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;SBOM generated through instrumenting the system running the software, to capture only components present in the system, as well as external call-outs or dynamically loaded components. In some contexts, this may also be referred to as an &quot;Instrumented&quot; or &quot;Dynamic&quot; SBOM.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Operations/Project node904
node904 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>Project</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Operations/Project' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Operations/Project</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Temporary endeavor with a beginning and an end and that must be used to create a unique product, service or result.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Temporary endeavor with a beginning and an end and that must be used to create a unique product, service or result.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;Temporary endeavor with a beginning and an end and that must be used to create a unique product, service or result.

Based on the Project Management Body of Knowledge (PMBOK), 3rd edition.

startTime is the time at which a project starts or is planned to start.
endTime is the time at which a project ends or is planned to end.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
